  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Proposed 3.3m Double Storey Front/Side Extension with Gable Roof ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its bulk, massing, scale, siting, and design, including the introduction of a fragmented roof form and lack of articulation to the northwest elevation, would result in a visually intrusive and discordant addition. The extension would disrupt the established uniformity and architectural coherence of the surrounding estate, particularly within a prominent location where the original bookend features have been consistently retained. The proposal would appear as an incongruous and unbalanced addition, harmful to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and the wider streetscene. The proposal is therefore considered contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)Policies D4&nbsp; of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2,&nbsp; DMD1, and DMD5 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
  ],
